stereo-layer (1.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libstereo-policy: one rule for every video player. The user's explicit
    choice of a packing, or STEREO_POLICY_USER_FORCE_2D (not 3D), comes before
    the stream's mark; swap eyes still reverses what was decided.
  * stereo_policy_video_views() tells full from half views by what the stream
    says: Matroska's one-plane display size (RFC 9559 section 18.10) and the
    H.265 upsampled_aspect_ratio_flag (D.3.16), then by shape.
    stereo_policy_matroska_plane() and Stereo::Video::matroskaPlane() undo
    the folding of the plane size into the sample aspect ratio by FFmpeg.
  * The shape rule is named: a single picture is 5:4 to 12:5
    (STEREO_POLICY_SINGLE_PICTURE_*), so a marked frame of that shape holds
    half views and a doubled one full views. The private 2.5 and 1.2 limits
    are gone.
  * stereo_policy_name_tag() and stereo_policy_video_layout_named() read the
    3D tag of a file name (3D, SBS, TAB, OU and their half and full forms,
    LR, RL) after the user's choice and the stream's marks and before the
    shape. stereo_policy_halves_test() compares the halves of a decoded frame
    for a bare 3D tag. Stereo::Video gets nameTag().
  * The 1.4 signatures and symbols stay.
  * Carries the anaglyph detector fix of the picture lane: both colour sides
    of the pair are required, so a red-on-grey 2D picture no longer counts as
    an anaglyph. The H.264 frame packing table is cited as D-8 in V15 and D-9
    in V16.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:40:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Quick item: the stereo and pictureSize properties say whether the policy
    made a pair of the source, on any output, and one view's size, so a QML
    client (the Stereo Image wallpaper) can keep its ordinary image path for
    ordinary pictures and fit a pair to its area.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:50:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A still picture with no mark is a side-by-side pair only when its pixels
    say so: stereo_policy_picture_pair_by_content() (libstereo-policy) and
    Picture::pairByContent() compare the two halves block by block, after a
    small horizontal shift and next to no vertical one. The shape rule only
    gates the pixel test, so phone photos (20:9), two-monitor screenshots and
    banners are no longer pairs. Marks, the user's choice and anaglyph
    detection are unchanged. A call point for the file-name tag reader is
    marked in the decision.
  * StereoPicture (Quick): on a screen that shows one eye the item draws the
    pair's left view and declares nothing, as documented; only a stereo or
    anaglyph output takes the pair. A pair with no surface of its own yet is
    drawn as its left view, not whole.
  * libstereo-layer1 depends on the libstereo-policy1 of the same build.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:50:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libstereo-policy1, libstereo-policy-dev: the stereo policy without Qt
    (marks, video packings, full or half views, shape rules, the user's
    correction), for a browser or a player; libstereo-layer1 builds on it
    and keeps its symbols.
  * The full or half views rule of video: side by side is full at a
    display aspect of 2.5 or more, top and bottom at 1.2 or less
    (Video::fullViews(), stereo_layer_video_full_views()).
  * The user's swap-eyes correction applies over the mark in the video
    policy too, and a correction stored with a file
    (user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes) applies in Picture::load() and
    Picture::loadPair().

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:20:05 -0300

stereo-layer (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the SVGStereo mark in gzip-compressed SVG files (.svgz) too.
  * Read the whole Stereo3DLayout set exactly (sideBySideQuincunx,
    anaglyphCyanRed, anaglyphGreenMagenta, frameSequential, blockLaced
    added); the layout enumeration gains SideBySideQuincunx,
    FrameSequential and BlockLaced after the existing values.
  * Unpack checkerboard pictures, and upconvert interleaved, checkerboard
    and quincunx views to the frame's size; such pictures are decoded at
    their own size before they are taken apart.
  * WidgetLayer::setKeepTransparency(): an adapter's picture can keep its
    clear parts clear (ARGB8888 buffers, no opaque region).
  * Build-Depends: zlib1g-dev.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:20:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Take a photograph for a pair by its shape only from 2:1 to 3.6:1, and
    never for top and bottom: panoramas and phone screenshots stay one
    picture.
  * Add Picture::loadPair() and Picture::sideBySide() for thumbnailers: the
    policy before any pixel is read, views decoded small, both side by side.
  * Read the proposed SVGStereo mark on an SVG's root element; an unmarked
    drawing is one picture.
  * A tooltip or a popup prepared for a stereo layer keeps the panel its
    style draws (rounded corners, a shadow).
  * Build-Depends: qt6-svg-plugins, for the SVG tests.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Stereo::Video and stereo_layer_video_layout(): the players' shared
    rule for video, with a frame taken for side by side by its shape alone
    only at three times as wide as high or more.
  * Build-Depends: kimageformat6-plugins, for the reader tests (MPO and JPS);
    without it they failed in a clean build environment.

